<supplementary-material content-type="local-data" id="figs1" position="float" orientation="portrait"><caption><title>Supplemental Figure 1</title><p><bold>Optimization of CHIP/Hsp70 NanoBiT constructs</bold>. HEK293 cells were transfected with all possible combinations of CHIP and Hsp70 fused to the LgBiT and SmBiT tags and with positive and negative controls (Promega). Tagging Hsp70 with an N-terminal LgBiT and tagging CHIP with an N-terminal SmBiT provided the optimal signal. CHIP, C terminus of Hsc70 interacting protein</p></caption><media xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="figs1.jpg" position="float" orientation="portrait"><?suppdata-name figs1.jpg?><?suppdata-size 640003?><?suppdata-md5 cfab7136b08b0718b5234025d24dec28?><?suppdata-image-server-status NEVER_LOAD?><?suppdata-mime-type image?><?suppdata-mime-sub-type jpeg?><?suppdata-cloudpmc-urn urn:app:e87f/9097460/cfab7136b08b/figs1.jpg?></media></supplementary-material>
</p></sec><ack id="ack0010"><sec id="sec6"><title>Author contributions</title><p id="p0190">A. U., K. F., Q. Z., J. B. S., C. T., S. A., E. T. W., E. P., C. K., S. C., T. M. D., P. G.-A., and K. M. S. formal analysis; A. U., K. F., Q. Z., J. B.S., C. T., S. A., E. T. W., E. P., C. K., S. C., T. M. D., P. G.-A., and K. M. S. investigation; J. C. S., R. C. P., N. G. B., D. Y., and K. M. S. project administration; J. C. S., R. C. P., N. G. B., D. Y., and K. M. S. funding acquisition; A. U. and K. M. S writing-original draft; A. U., K. F., Q. Z., J. B. S., C. T., S. A., E. T. W., E. P., C. K., S. C., T. M. D., P. G.-A., K. M. S, J. C. S., R. P., N. G. B., and D. Y. writing review and editing.</p></sec><sec id="sec7"><title>Funding and additional information</title><p id="p0195">This work was supported by the <funding-source id="gs1"><institution-wrap><institution-id institution-id-type="doi">10.13039/100000002</institution-id><institution>National Institutes of Health</institution></institution-wrap></funding-source> grants R35GM119544 and R01 NS112191, a Research Seed Grant from the <funding-source id="gs2"><institution-wrap><institution-id institution-id-type="doi">10.13039/100002243</institution-id><institution>National Ataxia Foundation</institution></institution-wrap></funding-source>, and a Translating <funding-source id="gs3"><institution-wrap><institution-id institution-id-type="doi">10.13039/100016652</institution-id><institution>Duke Health</institution></institution-wrap></funding-source> Award to K. M. S.; R35GM128855 to N. G. B; and R35GM128595 R. C. P.; and R01 AG066710 and R01AG061188 to J. C. S.</p></sec></ack></back></article>